Catalog data
------------

`data/catalog.json` is a pruned copy of the open provider/model catalog published
by models.dev:

  https://models.dev/api.json
  https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev

  models.dev — MIT License — Copyright (c) 2025 models.dev

The upstream repository holds one TOML file per provider
(`providers/<id>/provider.toml` and `providers/<id>/models/*.toml`); the JSON
endpoint used here is its built form. `data/catalog.json` keeps only the fields
this module needs, in the upstream field order, with the upstream values
untouched. Regenerate it with `node scripts/generate.ts --from-url` and see the
git history for the snapshot date.

Model and provider names, prices and capability flags are facts about
third-party services, reproduced from that catalog so a z1 graph can be built
offline. Check the upstream catalogue for the authoritative and current values.

`data/overrides.json` is hand-written: it lists API base URLs for providers whose
upstream entry has no `api` field, each with the documentation page it was taken
from.
